.TH PDB_RESOLVE_PROCEDURE_REF 3 2020-04-04 libpdb

.SH NAME
pdb_resolve_procedure_ref \- resolve a procedure reference to its definition

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <pdb.h>
.PP
.BI "int pdb_resolve_procedure_ref(void *" context ,
.BI "    uint32_t " global_record_offset ", struct pdb_procedure *" out );
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR pdb_resolve_procedure_ref ()
resolves the S_PROCREF or S_LPROCREF record that begins at
.I global_record_offset
in the global symbol record stream.
The offset must be the first byte of a record.
References carry a one-based module index and an unbiassed module stream
offset
.RI ( ibSym );
the offset is measured from the first byte of the module stream, including
its four-byte signature.
The referenced module and record are therefore required to exist, and the
record at
.I ibSym
must itself be the start of a symbol.
Identical offsets or names in other modules are not treated as identity.
.PP
S_PROCREF resolves to an S_GPROC32 record and S_LPROCREF resolves to an
S_LPROC32 record. The
.Fn _ID
and older ST record forms are not supported.
.PP
.nf
struct pdb_procedure {
    uint32_t module_index;     /* zero-based */
    uint32_t symbol_offset;    /* offset of the definition in its module stream */
    const char *name;          /* borrowed */
    uint16_t section;
    uint32_t address_offset;
    uint32_t code_size;
    uint32_t type_index;       /* not resolved */
    bool is_local;
};
.fi
.PP
.I type_index
is returned as stored; the type it names is not parsed by this call.
.I name
is borrowed from
.I context
and remains valid until
.BR pdb_reset_context (3),
a subsequent
.BR pdb_load (3),
or
.BR pdb_destroy_context (3).

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 on error. Outputs are cleared on failure.
Detailed error information can be retrieved with
.BR pdb_errno (3).

.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EPDB_NO_PDB_LOADED
No PDB file has been loaded into
.IR context .
.TP
.B EPDB_INVALID_PARAMETER
.I out
was NULL.
.TP
.B EPDB_NOT_FOUND
The PDB has no global record stream, so no procedure reference exists.
.TP
.B EPDB_UNSUPPORTED_VERSION
The record is not an S_PROCREF or S_LPROCREF, or its target is not an
S_GPROC32 or S_LPROC32.
.TP
.B EPDB_PARSE_ERROR
The offset is not a record boundary, the module index is invalid, or the
referenced offset does not begin a supported definition inside the module's
symbol region.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdb_get_modules (3),
.BR pdb_get_symbols (3),
.BR pdb_errno (3)
